      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Read matrix into flat array for better cache locality\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n\n    // Prefix sum array: (n+1) x (n+1), initialized to zero\n    std::vector<long long> pref((n + 1) * (n + 1), 0);\n\n    // Step 1: row-wise cumulative sums in parallel\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        int base_row = (i + 1) * (n + 1);   // pref[i+1][0]\n        int mat_row = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[mat_row + j];\n            pref[base_row + j + 1] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Step 2: column-wise accumulation in parallel over columns\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        int col_idx = j + 1;   // pref[0][col_idx] is zero\n        long long col_sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            col_sum += pref[i * (n + 1) + col_idx];\n            pref[i * (n + 1) + col_idx] = col_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Evaluate all SxS submatrix sums in O(1) each, vectorized\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max : mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        int base_i = i * (n + 1);\n        int base_is = (i + s) * (n + 1);\n#pragma omp simd\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            long long sum = pref[base_is + j + s]\n                          - pref[base_i + j + s]\n                          - pref[base_is + j]\n                          + pref[base_i + j];\n            if (sum > mxSum)\n                mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replace sliding-window algorithm with an optimized 2D prefix-sum (integral image) approach using OpenMP for parallel row-wise and column-wise accumulation. The final submatrix sum evaluation is a simple O(1) expression that is vectorized via #pragma omp simd, eliminating loop-carried dependencies of the original snake traversal. Memory layout uses a flat array with extra border to simplify indexing and improve cache locality.",
  "notes": "This approach reduces complexity from O(N^2 S) to O(N^2), enabling better vectorization. The final evaluation loop has no dependencies, allowing auto-vectorization by the compiler. Uses long long for intermediate sums to avoid overflow; result fits in int as guaranteed.",
